[8.630906, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[8.717191, "o", "\u001b[1;32m\r\n\u2713 Registered on http://relay:8766 \u2014 peers can message you.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.717273, "o", "\u001b[1;31m\r\n\u26a0 Keys are stored UNENCRYPTED \u2014 anyone who can read this folder can impersonate you.\r\n  Use --passphrase (or RETALK_PASSPHRASE) for any identity whose privacy matters.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nName:        alice\r\nPath:        ~/.retalk/alice\r\n"]
[8.71894, "o", "Fingerprint: 4bc48bc389cc613a7068d1d417f9fac2\r\nRelay:       http://relay:8766\r\n"]
[8.724148, "o", "\r\nTo INVITE a peer who is not on retalk yet, share this:\r\n\u001b[2m```bash\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# Let's talk over retalk, a CLI-based messaging\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# 1. Install retalk (if not installed yet):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36mpip install -U retalk               # or: uv add retalk\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# 2. Create your identity (pick any name; init also prints a reply to send me):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36mretalk init --relay http://relay:8766 --passphrase <PRIVATE-PASSPHRASE> # -u <your-username>\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# 3. Add me as a contact (specify your username for user-specific contact):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36mretalk add 4bc48bc389cc613a7068d1d417f9fac2 --peer alice --verify # -u <your-username>\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# 4. Send me the 'reply' block that step 2 printed, so I can add you back\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.729227, "o", "\r\nOr, if you are REPLYING to an invite someone sent you, send them this instead:\r\n\u001b[2m```bash\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# Got your invite for retalk.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# Add me back (specify your username for user-specific contact):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36mretalk add 4bc48bc389cc613a7068d1d417f9fac2 --peer alice --verify # --user <your-name>\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m# Then we can message each other.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
